The earlier finding ("`from_value` rebuilds only process/step/composite/binding") is **fully
closed** — all 12 kinds round-trip (process/step/composite/reaction/function/pattern/type/contract/
protocol/unit/context/binding). The premise the Stage-4 FLAT/RICH dissolution leans on —
definition-as-data uniform across kinds — is now TRUE, not just honest. unit/context reified via
STRUCTURAL `Dimension`/`UnitExpr`/`Ratio`/`ContextRule` codecs (surface AST in `ast.rs`, NO core
dependency — core's flagged Ratio-serde is for the LOWERED Schema path of #71, a different layer).
GROW_DIVIDE's `unit pg` now round-trips too (the lone remaining gap there, closed).
- **Build hygiene** — added `[profile.dev]` `debug = "line-tables-only"` + `incremental = false`
  to root `Cargo.toml` (the full 93-binary suite at default `debug = 2` filled the disk). Rule:
  `cargo check -p <crate>` / `cargo test -p <crate> --test <one>` — NEVER bare
  `cargo test -p chrysalis`. (Future structural win: consolidate the 93 `tests/*.rs` into a few
  binaries — coordinate w/ core+simplify.)

## Key gotchas (durable)
- **Codegen runner builds CONTEND on the shared `target/`.** A generated runner crate is
  `[workspace]`-isolated → it builds its deps under the DEFAULT `[profile.dev]` (≠ the repo's lean
  `debug = line-tables-only`), so its nested `cargo build` can invalidate/recompile shared artifacts
  + race the target lock against a concurrent workspace `cargo`. **SERIALIZE** codegen builds (don't
  overlap with `cargo check/test`); a transient `could not compile X (lib)` that VANISHES on an
  isolated retry is this contention, not a real error (hit during P5c-1, confirmed harmless). The
  real target is `/mnt/data/archive/prism-target` (`.cargo/config.toml`); `run_structured` finds it
  via `cargo metadata` now (was a hardcoded `workspace/target`, which missed the relocated rlibs).
  The human + `unify` are looking at AUTOMATING the `build:` lease/broadcast (a PreToolUse/PostToolUse
  hook on `cargo build|test` → `coord set build.state=…`).
- **Build = disk.** One shared `target/` (no worktrees) — cargo's lock serializes agents, so the
  pain is SIZE (debug symbols × 93 test binaries) + cross-agent rebuilds of shared crates. Lean
  profile + targeted `--test` keep it bounded. `cargo clean` on the shared target forces EVERYONE
  to full-rebuild — prefer `cargo clean -p <crate>` or `rm -rf target/debug/{incremental,examples}`.
- **Two reaction wrappings (don't conflate):** `build_reaction_value` returns the chrysalis `Rule`
  (`Foreign(FOREIGN_RULE)`) so a LOCAL BRS binds this evaluator (computed reactums + closure);
  `eval_rule_expr`/`compile_reaction` REIFY to `Foreign(FOREIGN_REACTION)` (transmittable, rules-as-
  state). `build_rule` is the shared LOWERING; the wrapping is the caller's choice.
